.parquet

This template reads an s3:// parquet address in `_file` itself (D1486):
reader.py registers an fsspec filesystem over shared/remote_range.py with
DuckDB, so a page reads the footer and the row groups and columns it shows
from a URL the server signs, never the whole object. Only parquet streams:
CSV/JSON have no footer to page from. Lines starting with "." list the
extensions it streams.
